---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import PageHeader from '../components/PageHeader.astro';
import { SITE } from '../lib/site';
import { breadcrumb, webPage } from '../lib/schema';

const title = 'Privacy Policy';
const description =
	'How VendorDesk handles your data: every calculation and PDF happens in your browser. We never transmit, save or store your figures, clients or dimensions.';
const updated = '6 September 2026';

const schema = [
	webPage({ name: `${title} · ${SITE.name}`, path: '/privacy-policy', description, hasBreadcrumb: true }),
	breadcrumb([
		{ name: 'Home', path: '/' },
		{ name: 'Privacy Policy', path: '/privacy-policy' },
	]),
];
---

<Layout title={title} description={description} schema={schema}>
	<PageHeader
		eyebrow="Legal"
		title="Privacy Policy"
		lead="The short version: your inputs stay on your device. This page explains exactly what that means and what little we do collect."
		crumbs={[{ name: 'Home', href: '/' }, { name: 'Privacy Policy' }]}
	>
		<p class="mt-6 text-caption text-ink-3">Last updated {updated}</p>
	</PageHeader>

	<section class="bg-canvas">
		<div class="mx-auto max-w-prose px-5 py-16 sm:px-8 sm:py-24">
			<div class="rich-text">
				<p class="callout">
					<strong>All mathematical calculations and PDF generations happen locally in your web browser. VendorDesk does not
					transmit, save, or store your financial inputs, client names, or packaging dimensions on any server.</strong>
				</p>

				<h2>1. Who we are</h2>
				<p>
					This website, {SITE.legalName} (“VendorDesk”, “we”, “us”), is an independent collection of browser-based utilities
					for businesses and designers. You can contact us at <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>.
				</p>

				<h2>2. Data you enter into our tools</h2>
				<p>
					Our tools — including the Paper Bag Dieline Generator and the Bill of Supply Generator — are implemented entirely as
					client-side JavaScript. When you type dimensions, business details, client details, item descriptions or amounts,
					that information is processed by your own browser to draw the preview, calculate results and build the SVG, PNG or
					PDF file you download.
				</p>
				<ul>
					<li>Your inputs are <strong>not sent to VendorDesk</strong>, our hosting provider, or any third party.</li>
					<li>We have <strong>no database</strong> of user inputs and no accounts, because none are needed.</li>
					<li>Files you download are created in your browser’s memory and saved directly to your device.</li>
				</ul>

				<h2>3. Information stored on your device</h2>
				<p>
					To make the tools more convenient, some pages use your browser’s <em>local storage</em> to remember settings on
					your own device, for example:
				</p>
				<ul>
					<li>Your light or dark theme preference.</li>
					<li>The last dimensions and options you used in the dieline generator.</li>
					<li>A draft of your Bill of Supply so you can return to it later, if you choose to keep drafts.</li>
				</ul>
				<p>
					This data never leaves your browser and is not visible to us. You can delete it at any time using the “Reset” or
					“Clear draft” controls on the tool pages, or by clearing your browser’s site data for this website.
				</p>

				<h2>4. Server logs</h2>
				<p>
					Like virtually every website, the infrastructure that serves our static files may automatically record standard
					technical information about requests — such as the page requested, the date and time, your IP address, browser
					type and referring page — for security, abuse prevention and capacity planning. These logs are not linked to any
					tool inputs (which, again, are never transmitted) and are retained only for as long as the hosting provider’s
					standard retention period.
				</p>

				<h2>5. Cookies and advertising</h2>
				<p>
					VendorDesk itself does not set tracking cookies. To keep the tools free, we may display advertising provided by
					third-party advertising networks such as Google AdSense. Where advertising is shown:
				</p>
				<ul>
					<li>Third-party vendors, including Google, may use cookies or similar identifiers to serve ads based on your prior visits to this or other websites.</li>
					<li>Google’s use of advertising cookies enables it and its partners to serve ads based on your visit to this site and/or other sites on the Internet.</li>
					<li>You may opt out of personalised advertising by visiting <a href="https://www.google.com/settings/ads" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Ads Settings</a> or <a href="https://www.aboutads.info/choices/" rel="noopener noreferrer">aboutads.info</a>.</li>
				</ul>
				<p>
					Any advertising is served in separate page areas and has no access to the contents of the tools or the data you
					enter into them.
				</p>

				<h2>6. Analytics</h2>
				<p>
					We do not run analytics or session-recording scripts on the tool inputs. If we introduce privacy-respecting,
					aggregate page-view analytics in the future, this policy will be updated before it goes live.
				</p>

				<h2>7. Email</h2>
				<p>
					If you write to us, we will use your email address and message solely to reply to you. Our contact form opens your
					own email application; it does not submit anything to our servers.
				</p>

				<h2>8. Children</h2>
				<p>VendorDesk is a business utility and is not directed at children under 16. We do not knowingly collect personal data from children.</p>

				<h2>9. Your rights</h2>
				<p>
					Because we do not hold your tool data, there is nothing for us to access, correct or delete on your behalf — it is
					already under your control on your own device. For anything relating to email correspondence or server logs, you
					can contact us at <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a> and we will respond in line with applicable
					law, including India’s Digital Personal Data Protection Act, 2023.
				</p>

				<h2>10. Changes to this policy</h2>
				<p>
					We may update this policy as the site evolves. The “last updated” date at the top of this page will change when we
					do, and material changes will be summarised here.
				</p>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>
</Layout>
